  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3790",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with potassium channels through a shared mechanism involving delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6, Kcnv2, or Kcna7, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, which in turn is associated with Kcns3. This indicates a potential pathway where Guanidine may modulate potassium channel function, leading to changes in Kcns3 activity. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact mechanism of how Guanidine influences the channel activity remains to be fully elucidated. The overlapping roles of these potassium channels in delayed rectifier activity imply that Guanidine may exert its effects through a common pathway, possibly by altering channel gating or conformation.",
